  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_25d0e869d5a34c9bb6f72147c0aeefe5",
      "statement": "The per-stack dev-credential contract is two files per stack for the four named stacks (auth, mcm, audit, observability): a committed `infrastructure-as-code/docker/stacks/<stack>.env.example` placeholder template and a gitignored `<stack>.env` holding the generated real values that Compose reads. The template uses `NAME=<generate:KIND>` for a freshly minted value and `NAME=literal` for a deterministic fixture.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/stacks/README.md",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:ecc1411123c4003e5f27ba22223197b2da0584d593e324cbc938c06eb07a50e7"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/gen-dev-secrets.mjs#L1-L25",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0fce06e6a96399b2505038b5ef60de91d0116621b8cc368b44f8e5129dd058ce:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c23666af0222432a9e54600f5083c198",
      "statement": "The generated `<stack>.env` reaches Compose through two distinct paths: the stack aggregator's long-syntax `include:` with an explicit `env_file:` pin on the specific included component files that need it (auth pins keycloak and vault, mcm pins agent-db and agent-gateway, audit pins opensearch, observability pins observability), and the Nx `up-*`/`down-*` targets' `--env-file` argument for the whole compose invocation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/stacks/audit.compose.yaml#L10-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:677fad2172c62af98bfdc94779ee7210838165a395298bb5d9bfa1262bee4c0e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/stacks/auth.compose.yaml#L14-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cd55289dbca8678d68c424c1654788fe5ea8d562389f48351b4a3f8b83c1cfbc:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/stacks/mcm.compose.yaml#L34-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d2b054ec26a30d212ac5618cc09b64a19e050c4da7f3277e2be6e7cec82edeb0:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/stacks/observability.compose.yaml#L11-L15",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c8b40c0623540e502d637aad231fde9ab8efc2cb9accf5bfdd350fa32763ccfd:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/project.json#L6-L55",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1fc35f74918b8b187af5fa04b52afb214ea82539808eaa0d63b52839cc1dca8f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cce8ab0fb8544f9ca52d7c140d31da3b",
      "statement": "Every credential in a tracked compose file is a fail-fast `${VAR:?…}` interpolation reference, so a missing or blank value makes `docker compose up`/`config` abort naming the variable and the per-stack env file that should hold it, rather than starting a half-configured stack.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/agent-gateway/compose.yaml#L22-L22",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e54d09a956aa886221db5652c7c7c2814958f1a3c892838efc20948a0027572a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/keycloak/compose.yaml#L15-L16",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5e7f351dbc05ce71f7f9779057cc96ede53a1e96374d373a3243a31ff2a23f3d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/stacks/README.md",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:ecc1411123c4003e5f27ba22223197b2da0584d593e324cbc938c06eb07a50e7"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7fd99d176d2f46d9bb426504d8db2553",
      "statement": "`scripts/gen-dev-secrets.mjs` mints each `<generate:KIND>` placeholder with the kind's alphabet and shape — b62-32/b62-48 (URL/shell-safe base62), hex-64 (32 bytes as hex), complex-16 (upper+lower+digit+special from a URL/shell-safe set), unleash-admin/unleash-client (token prefixes plus a base62 body), and mongo-keyfile (single-line base64 of the MongoDB replica-set keyfile content) — using `node:crypto` with rejection sampling to avoid modulo bias, and treats an unknown kind as a hard error naming the key rather than writing an empty value.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/gen-dev-secrets.mjs#L27-L95",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9fbcaddd1ab213d408bf9e86b41bed0e7eb58ce5716fad08ef1d247da358caff:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c918248c292a4a5fa932d97f8cbb8f40",
      "statement": "The generator's idempotent path is a back-fill, not a plain skip: for an existing `<stack>.env` it seeds keys the template has gained and mints in place any `<generate:KIND>` key that is present but empty, while leaving every existing value — including hand-edited ones — byte-for-byte untouched, because the only alternative for delivering one new variable would be `--force`, which rotates every other value and takes the running stacks down.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/gen-dev-secrets.mjs#L176-L184",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:81d0a1374753ee9a1af77de16bf55536e40c402cf589c16a28249dfb656e26fb:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/gen-dev-secrets.mjs#L97-L167",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1a8dd73d6f86170c35e9b998e0b73727a5ea568be796883678a448980ad7febd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_29a4b6b047eb4c22a35e51d7ad6f6836",
      "statement": "A key the template deliberately leaves blank is not treated as a gap: `REGISTRY_HOST` is empty in the mcm and observability templates because `scripts/check-topology-scrub.mjs` forbids a real tailnet host in a committed file, so it is set per machine and the compose image references fail loudly naming the variable instead of resolving to an invalid image reference.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/stacks/mcm.env.example#L31-L38",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:30e3078009b4dd0ac4a4cd18110f1972743e4320ec592d2c9b34a65a4881ee9d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/stacks/observability.env.example#L24-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:42adaaf348b01d6cc14f536f32542929501a5d0dce21092286b77c827f89a00f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/check-topology-scrub.mjs#L1-L40",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:64eb801aae6ea84f4c914a7ff3698cc3f3a51b1bd19fd7a48afa6920e41deaea:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_140bb82dba014873acb094bb43660949",
      "statement": "Deterministic fixtures are copied verbatim from the template and survive `--force`: the two LangFuse `LANGFUSE_INIT_PROJECT_*` keys are fixed because the agent gateway and a verify test authenticate against those exact values, and the fixed public halves of the backup-destination fixtures (S3 access key, WebDAV username) are fixed so the integration suite can name them without reading the env file.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/stacks/mcm.env.example#L22-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2d206816ef792754fe1585da005ab2c0f9712e6baf979be9bba18339048bd49b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/stacks/observability.env.example#L19-L22",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:16610c41f0d55bc7fc6be881dd79b2d56b1ff5bf321ddeda788a179a747fc426:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/gen-dev-secrets.mjs#L200-L215",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7a9427de506d0830c052b8e45bc2b1685fd0fd865bd0ec6eb0a48173b94f51b3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7afc76788e4a46a3a201805f96380c02",
      "statement": "Password-on-first-init credentials (Postgres, OpenSearch, MinIO) bake their value into the data volume on first init and ignore later env changes, so rotating the `.env` requires recreating the service with a fresh volume or the container keeps the volume's original password and auth fails; Redis values, Unleash tokens and app secrets have no such persistence and rotate on a plain restart.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/local-dev.md",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:2d3f8aaaad311599478088314db9fa3544b4510ad9abf00e62383c4d944953a4"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/stacks/auth.env.example#L10-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c14f165cebd9f77f1249e4a966ae9145d1c5a21e5f57331562c43199344e86da:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e416c3138cc9414682b0e1e91bb0e0f4",
      "statement": "A container started before a re-run does not hold a newly minted value, so the services that consume it must be recreated and `node scripts/gen-dev-env.mjs` re-run to project the value into the BFF env files; the generator says so in its output rather than leaving the next 401 to be diagnosed from scratch.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/gen-dev-env.mjs#L1-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:36b233b94f52e3c3e69d69cae2f531eb2f51a6ebc2f79bac3ec3f0fa627fdcd7:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/gen-dev-secrets.mjs#L159-L166",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3b2deefe78519cd2f88542fd89d4fe9d06806a7f0ad15f894e72218e9ad25ba0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_189f6bc1a7914d36bfb3b8ea36a7df2c",
      "statement": "The generator prints key NAMES only and never values, and a guard test enforces this by asserting that no non-trivial value in the written file appears anywhere in the generator's combined stdout/stderr.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/__tests__/gen-dev-secrets.guard.test.mjs#L71-L110",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1440a3b08921bd8f1494b14627a3c0b903adf9847d7d6421eaf61fd1652882dd:"
